Title:          qmplay2.tcz
Description:    QT5 alsa,pipewire or pulseaudio media player 
                audio or video player for X or wayland 
Version:        24.04.07 
Author:         https://github.com/zaps166/QMPlay2/blob/master/AUTHORS
Original-site:  https://github.com/zaps166/QMPlay2
Copying-policy: LGPL v3
Size:           2.5M
Extension_by:   aus9 @linuxquestions.org
Tags:           audio video player alsa pulseaudio pipewire youtube    
Comments:       Set up your sound device first, may need more TCEs. I added
                pulseaudio and pipewire support but only tested alsa and pipewire.
                For alsa volume control I use alsamixer from alsa TCE.
                For pipewire I used pavucontrol but please read info files for
                pipewire or pulseaudio please. 

                Can play most formats and has a YouTube browser. For max video choices 
                boot into 3d or a suitable wayland desktop. Load optional vulkan-tools 
                and read the info file if that interests you.
                
                qmplay2 supports spherical view on OpenGL and Vulkan video outputs. 
                Search in youtube TAB for 360 degree or sperical
                Pressing "Ctrl+3" or Playback->Video filters->Spherical view
                -> mouse pointer changes to either a "grabbable hand"  or 4 arrows etc

                To play audio cd -> Playlist (or Alt + P)..Click "+"  select audiocd 
                DVDs not supported. 
                                                                
                Searching Youtubes will pause this playback to download its own yt-dlp to
                ~/.config/QMPlay2 where other files can be found, including log.
                While playing a youtube, you can click context menu, RH click for RH 
                mouse user and choose to download your track. Note that pressing the 
                normal stop button stops playing a track. To stop downloading you need
                to click into the downloader TAB and click the "icon" to the right of 
                download at the top.
              
                Tested internet radios mp3 and aac streams OK

                Note there are so many settings to turn on/off hardware/software/modules
                ....take your time having a look before requesting help please.
                eg pulseaudio module was turned off first startup for me YMMV

